    "narrative": "For June 23, 2026, the Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored by **Mickey Moniak** (74.73) and **Josh Naylor** (72.86). **Mickey Moniak** serves as our primary offensive engine today, benefiting from a massive 14% boost due to a favorable park and platoon alignment against Gray, while **Josh Naylor** capitalizes on the favorable wind out conditions and a strong matchup against M. Keller. Similarly, **Corbin Carroll** remains an elite start at 72.25; even with a neutral park factor, his high-floor speed profile and the advantageous platoon split against Leahy make him a mandatory fixture for our pursuit of the scarcity-driven SB category.\n\nTactical edge-seeking defines the middle of the order, specifically with **Tyler Soderstrom** (62.76) and **Brice Turang** (63.21). **Tyler Soderstrom** benefits significantly from wind conditions and an advantageous matchup against the vulnerable arm of Ray, while **Brice Turang** provides essential stability with a robust 8% boost from his #2 lineup spot. The most difficult personnel decision involved **Zach McKinstry**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 51.70 score. While his platoon edge against Rod\u00f3n was enticing, his low spot in the batting order ultimately pushed his projected efficiency below that of **Max Muncy** and **Alex Freeland**, whose underlying skill matchups against Ray and K. Rojas offered slightly higher statistical outcomes.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given the current board. **James Wood** (54.85) is a high-upside play, but his score is suppressed by Luzardo\u2019s elite holding ability, which severely limits his stolen base ceiling today. While his 0.404 xwOBA keeps him relevant, we are monitoring the threat of his matchup closely. Furthermore, **Austin Riley** (58.01) sees his score docked by a late-order placement and W. Peralta\u2019s slow delivery, which ironically presents a unique opportunity for him to exploit the catcher's arm. We have maintained a disciplined stance on benching players like **Jose Caballero** and **Travis Bazzana** to preserve game caps, banking on the daily efficiency models to outperform raw volume in this pivotal mid-season stretch.",
